Yes, that works and keeps the relay small:
- the login page takes the face name; the relay mails a short code to that member stored email and answers with a form for the code;
- the member row holds only a hash of the code and its expiry (about 10 minutes, one use);
- a right code opens a session: a random cookie kept in the relay memory, never on disk, so a relay restart just means logging in again.
The one new need: the relay must send mail, through an SMTP account or a mail API whose key sits in this goal store, the relay owner one.
